course: dictionary
lesson: 5230
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word jersey is a good example: it can mean a piece of clothing, a sports shirt, a place, or a cow. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. These are its context, and they give you clues.
explain: «A boy in New Jersey saw a car hit a bike and drive away.» Here Jersey has a capital letter and comes after New. That tells you it is a place, a state in the USA, not a top you wear. Capital letters are a clue too.
explain: «...a faded blue jersey and his things tied up in a blue handkerchief.» Faded and blue describe something you can wear, and the handkerchief sits beside it, so jersey means a knitted top, like a jumper. Always check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A jersey can be a knitted top with sleeves, like a jumper or sweater.
fact: A jersey can also be a shirt worn by players in a sports team, often with a number on it.
fact: Jersey is an island in the English Channel, and a Jersey is a breed of cow from there.
fact: In New Zealand and Australia, a jersey is the usual word for a jumper; in the USA and Canada, a jersey usually means a sports shirt.
fact: Jersey is a Crown Dependency, not part of the UK, and New Jersey is a state in the USA named after the island.
exercise: «A boy in New Jersey saw a car hit a bike and drive away.» In this sentence, what is Jersey? | A knitted top | A sports shirt with a number | A breed of cow | *A place, a state in the USA
exercise: «...a faded blue jersey and his things tied up in a blue handkerchief.» What does jersey mean here? | A hat | An island in the English Channel | A sports shirt with a number | *A knitted top, like a jumper
exercise: The players ran onto the pitch in their new football jerseys. What is a jersey here? | A cow from the island of Jersey | A knitted top with sleeves for winter | *A shirt worn by a player in a team | A soft stretchy cloth
test: «Jersey is a Crown Dependency, not part of the UK.» In this sentence, what is Jersey? | A breed of cow | A jumper | *An island | A sports shirt
test: A New Zealander says, «Grab your jersey, it's cold outside.» What does jersey mean? | *A jumper | An island | A sports shirt | A football with a number
exam: In «a faded blue jersey», what helps show that jersey means clothing? | The word lane | *The word faded, which describes a worn colour on something you wear | The word rat | The word traveller
